## Summary

Audited main at 7ce5c40 for structural complexity across server wiring, store transactions/queues, generated memberships, search indexing, document workers, share pages, tool responses and shared browser utilities. Selected one bounded cleanup.

Before: internal/db/effective.go maintained generatedSet.ready separately from its built index map, with assignments in both the request builder and background warmer.
Now: the presence of the index map determines readiness, removing redundant state and its update sites. The map is initialized even for empty generated tables; locking and nonblocking warming retain their behavior. Updated the existing warmer test to inspect that map directly.

Focused existing tests for membership caching/invalidation, warming, generated birthdays and the search table passed, as did go vet ./... and git diff --check. Review completed with no findings. The requested merge from main reported already up to date and required no conflict resolution.

Deliberately left per-app redirect/presentation contracts intact and avoided a shared picture/search queue abstraction because their scheduling and invalidation requirements differ. No schema changes or production writes.

## Reviews

### Snapshot #1, reviewer "Review", grok grok-4.7: done

The generated-table cache used a separate `ready` flag to mean the set had been built. `build` always assigns `by` to a non-nil index map when it finishes, so the flag duplicated that fact. Callers now treat a nil `by` as unbuilt, in both the on-demand path and the warmer, and the existing warmer test checks that same condition.

No significant findings.
